---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ArrowLeft, ExternalLink } from 'lucide-react';
import { CONFERENCE_DETAILS } from '../constants';
---

<BaseLayout title="About - AI Engineering Code Summit">
  <div class="w-full min-h-screen bg-paper pb-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto bg-[#fdfdfc] border-x border-void min-h-screen shadow-lg">

      <!-- Toolbar -->
      <div class="sticky top-0 z-40 bg-paper border-b border-void p-3 flex justify-between items-center print:hidden border-x border-void mx-[-1px]">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="flex items-center gap-2 text-void hover:text-rand-blue transition-colors font-mono font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-widest px-2"
        >
          <ArrowLeft class="w-4 h-4" />
          Back to Summary
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Page Content -->
      <div class="px-8 md:px-24 py-16">

        <!-- Header Block -->
        <div class="mb-12 border-b-4 border-void pb-8">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-gray-500 block mb-2">Project Documentation</span>
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-sans font-black text-void leading-none uppercase mb-6">
            About This Report
          </h1>
          <p class="font-mono text-sm text-gray-600">
            Comprehensive analysis and synthesis from the AI Engineer Code Summit 2025
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Content -->
        <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-sans prose-headings:font-black prose-headings:uppercase prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-h2:text-3xl prose-h2:mt-16 prose-h2:mb-6 prose-h3:text-2xl prose-h3:mt-12 prose-h3:mb-4 prose-p:font-mono prose-p:text-lg prose-p:leading-8 prose-p:my-6 prose-ul:my-6 prose-li:my-3 prose-li:font-mono prose-li:text-lg prose-li:leading-8 prose-ol:my-6 prose-ol:my-3 prose-blockquote:border-l-4 prose-blockquote:border-rand-blue prose-blockquote:pl-6 prose-blockquote:py-4 prose-blockquote:my-10 prose-blockquote:font-sans prose-blockquote:text-xl prose-blockquote:leading-9 prose-blockquote:font-bold prose-blockquote:not-italic prose-a:text-rand-blue prose-a:font-semibold prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline">

          <h2>The Conference</h2>
          <p>
            The <strong>AI Engineer Code Summit 2025</strong> took place November 19-22, 2025 in Midtown Manhattan, New York.
            This report covers the Leadership Sessions (November 20) and Engineering Sessions (November 21).
          </p>

          <p>
            This single-track, invite-only conference brought together top AI engineers building coding agents and
            AI-powered development tools from leading organizations.
          </p>

          <div class="border-l-4 border-rand-blue pl-6 py-4 my-8 bg-gray-50">
            <p class="font-sans font-bold text-base mb-2">Conference Website</p>
            <a href="https://www.ai.engineer/code" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm">
              ai.engineer/code <ExternalLink class="w-3 h-3" />
            </a>
          </div>

          <h2>Featured Organizations</h2>
          <p>The summit included practitioners from:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>OpenAI</strong> - Bill Chen, Brian Fioca, Will Hang, Cathy Zhou</li>
            <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> - Barry Zhang, Mahesh Murag, Katelyn Lesse</li>
            <li><strong>Google/DeepMind</strong> - Kat Kampf, Ammaar Reshi, Kevin Hou, Jed Borovik</li>
            <li><strong>Meta</strong> - Jacob Kahn</li>
            <li><strong>Netflix</strong> - Jake Nations</li>
            <li><strong>Replit</strong> - Michele Catasta</li>
            <li><strong>Factory AI</strong> - Eno Reyes</li>
            <li>And many others from Cursor, Prime Intellect, Browser Company, McKinsey, Bloomberg, Capital One, Northwestern Mutual</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>What's Inside</h2>
          <p>This report documents two days of intensive technical sessions analyzing:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Agent architectures and production harnesses</li>
            <li>Context management and memory systems</li>
            <li>Trust and evaluation frameworks</li>
            <li>Economics and ROI of AI engineering</li>
            <li>Developer experience patterns</li>
            <li>Infrastructure and tooling evolution</li>
          </ul>

          <h3>Key Outputs</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>40+ individual session notes with embedded slides</li>
            <li>11 major themes identified across both days</li>
            <li>13,000+ words of detailed analysis</li>
            <li>50+ speaker profiles and research notes</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>How to Use This Report</h2>
          <p>
            This site is organized into two main tracks that mirror the conference structure:
          </p>

          <div class="not-prose grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8">
            <a href="/track/leadership" class="border-2 border-void p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors group">
              <h3 class="font-sans font-black text-xl uppercase mb-2 group-hover:text-rand-blue">Leadership Track</h3>
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-600">6 themes exploring organizational strategy, trust, economics, and the evolving role of software development in the AI era.</p>
            </a>

            <a href="/track/engineering" class="border-2 border-void p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors group">
              <h3 class="font-sans font-black text-xl uppercase mb-2 group-hover:text-rand-blue">Engineering Track</h3>
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-600">5 themes covering technical architecture, agent harnesses, code quality, observability, and infrastructure patterns.</p>
            </a>
          </div>

          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-500 border-t border-gray-300 pt-6">
            Navigate using the tabs above to explore themes, speakers, and sessions. Use the FILES button to save items for later review.
          </p>

          <h2>Analysis Methodology</h2>
          <p>
            All analysis and synthesis in this report was generated using <strong>Claude Code</strong> with custom
            conference analysis workflows. The process involved:
          </p>
          <ol>
            <li>Session-by-session note transcription with slide integration</li>
            <li>Thematic pattern identification across sessions</li>
            <li>Cross-referencing speaker insights and key concepts</li>
            <li>Synthesis of major themes with supporting evidence</li>
            <li>Executive summary and presentation deck generation</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>About the Author</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>Will Schenk</strong> is a father, entrepreneur, technologist and aspiring woodsman living in the
            woods of Northwest Connecticut with his wife Ksenia, four boys, and one baby girl.
          </p>

          <p>
            In 2010, Will cofounded <a href="https://www.crunchbase.com/person/will-schenk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HappyFunCorp</a>,
            a software development company focused on mobile product development. He stepped back from day-to-day operations
            in January 2022 and sold the company later that year. He then took a professional break from technology, moved
            to the woods to focus on family, and started Cornwall Market, a brick and mortar food market.
          </p>

          <p>
            During his break, the world of generative AI emerged, drawing him back to the tech space. He founded
            <a href="https://thefocus.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Focus AI</a> in November 2024,
            working with clients to apply AI technology in real-world scenarios and exploring practical implementations
            of AI in software development.
          </p>

          <div class="border border-gray-300 p-6 my-8 bg-white">
            <p class="font-sans font-bold text-sm uppercase mb-3">Connect</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1">
              <li><a href="https://willschenk.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center gap-2">Website: willschenk.com <ExternalLink class="w-3 h-3" /></a></li>
              <li><a href="https://github.com/wschenk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center gap-2">GitHub: @wschenk <ExternalLink class="w-3 h-3" /></a></li>
              <li><a href="https://x.com/wschenk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center gap-2">Twitter/X: @wschenk <ExternalLink class="w-3 h-3" /></a></li>
              <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/will-schenk-420266/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="flex items-center gap-2">LinkedIn: Will Schenk <ExternalLink class="w-3 h-3" /></a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="border-l-4 border-alert-red pl-6 py-4 my-8 bg-gray-50">
            <p class="font-sans font-bold text-sm uppercase mb-2">Document Reference</p>
            <p class="font-mono text-xs">
              DOC. NO: RM-2025-HZ<br/>
              PROJECT: AI Engineering Code Summit 2025<br/>
              CLASSIFICATION: UNCLASSIFIED
            </p>
          </div>

        </article>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
